window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"cloud-environments\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">云端环境</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在页面 URL 后追加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex Cloud 会在云端运行编程任务，因此即使你的电脑处于休眠状态，工作仍可继续。你可以在网页、移动应用或桌面应用中使用它来编辑代码、运行命令和检查结果。</p> <p><strong>云端环境</strong>是任务要使用的一套可重复利用的配置，包括代码库、依赖项、工具和访问设置。Codex 会检查你的代码库、准备环境并与你一起测试。每个新任务都会从已发布的环境创建一个独立、隔离的工作区。</p> <p>入门介绍请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud 概述</a>。</p> <p><strong>Codex Cloud（旧版）</strong>继续支持代码审查，以及 Linear 和 GitHub 集成。我们计划弃用此体验。有关为这些工作流程创建和管理环境，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">旧版指南</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"start-a-task-in-codex-cloud\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cloud\">在 Codex Cloud 中开始任务</h2> <p>在网页或<a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">桌面应用</a>中，选择 <strong>Work in（工作位置）&gt; Cloud（云端）</strong>，然后选择一个已发布的环境。在移动设备上，打开 <strong>Codex</strong> 并选择一个已发布的环境。描述你希望 Codex 完成的任务并发送请求。如果需要新的配置，请在网页或桌面应用中<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">创建环境</a>。</p> <p>Enterprise 管理员可以在推出 Codex Cloud 前<a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=step-5-configure-codex-cloud\">检查工作区访问权限</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"create-and-publish-an-environment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">创建并发布环境</h2> <p>请在网页或<a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">桌面应用</a>中新建环境，然后使用 ChatGPT 账户登录：</p> <ol> <li>在新任务中，选择 <strong>Work in（工作位置）&gt; Cloud（云端）</strong>，打开 <strong>Select environment（选择环境）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Create environment（创建环境）</strong>。</li> <li>选择要检出的 GitHub 代码库。如果系统提示，请连接 GitHub。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Get started（开始）</strong>。Codex 会检查代码库、安装依赖项和工具，并测试工作流程。</li> <li>系统询问时，补充缺失的访问权限或信息。你也可以指定版本、命令或服务。</li> <li>检查设置报告、配置和文件。完成尚未处理的工作，保存更改，然后选择 <strong>Publish（发布）</strong>。</li> <li>出现 <strong>Environment published（环境已发布）</strong> 后，选择 <strong>Start a new task（开始新任务）</strong>，并描述你希望 Codex 完成的工作。</li> </ol> <p>你也可以从 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Codex Cloud &gt; Environments（环境）&gt; Create environment（创建环境）</strong> 开始。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：桌面应用的环境选择器，其中列有“创建环境”和“管理环境”，位于已保存的环境列表下方。</p> </blockquote> <p>保存会存储配置；部分设置会立即应用到当前环境。发布会为新任务保存已准备好的文件系统快照。分享设置用于控制谁可以使用该环境。</p> <p><a id=\"default-universal-image\"></a> <a id=\"automatic-setup\"></a> <a id=\"manual-setup\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"customize-installation-and-startup\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">自定义安装和启动</h2> <p>Codex 会从你的代码库识别运行时、软件包版本、工具和服务。你可以在对话中调整配置，不必自己编写安装脚本。</p> <p>Codex 可以将测试过的配置记录在两个字段中：</p> <ul> <li><strong>安装脚本（Install script）：</strong> 用于安装依赖项和准备开发资源的命令。</li> <li><strong>启动技能（Start skill）：</strong> 用于启动服务并检查服务是否已就绪的指示。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>插图：云端环境设置对话旁显示代码库、脚本、网络、机密信息、变量、隐私和“高级”控制项，并提供“保存草稿”和“发布”操作。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"container-caching\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"reuse-and-update-saved-state\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">重用和更新已保存状态</h2> <ul> <li><strong>新任务：</strong> 从已发布环境中准备好的文件系统开始。</li> <li><strong>已有任务：</strong> 继续使用任务自己的已保存文件，包括未提交的更改和已安装的工具。</li> <li><strong>代码库刷新：</strong> 在后台自动运行，并保留依赖缓存；不会重新运行安装或启动命令。</li> </ul> <p>要更新可重用的配置，请打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Codex Cloud &gt; Environments（环境）</strong>。在环境的 <strong>…</strong> 菜单中选择 <strong>Edit（编辑）</strong>。描述所需更改，让 Codex 准备并测试配置，保存更改，然后选择 <strong>Republish（重新发布）</strong>。新任务会使用更新后的环境；已有任务保留各自的状态。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：Codex Cloud 设置页面中打开了 Environments（环境）和 Personal vault（个人保险库）标签页，并展开某个已发布环境的“编辑”菜单。</p> </blockquote> <p>请提交重要工作，或保存你需要的输出。已保存的状态不能取代源代码管理。</p> <p><a id=\"give-setup-access-to-private-dependencies\"></a> <a id=\"prepare-access-to-dependencies-and-services\"></a> <a id=\"environment-variables-and-secrets\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">配置环境变量和网络机密</h2> <p>Codex 会识别缺失的配置，并询问它无法推断出的值。在环境配置中，选择 <strong>Environment variables（环境变量）</strong> 或 <strong>Network secrets（网络机密）</strong> 旁边的 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong>。为每个值选择提供方式：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>配置项</th> <th>用途</th> <th>传递方式</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>环境变量</td> <td>程序需要直接读取的值</td> <td>直接传递给环境中的程序。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>网络机密</td> <td>发送到特定 HTTPS 服务的凭据</td> <td>程序收到的是占位符；代理会为允许访问的目标地址替换为真实值。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>配置网络机密时，请填写 <strong>Key（键）</strong>、<strong>Value（值）</strong> 和 <strong>Allowed domains（允许的域名）</strong>。请勿与直接变量使用相同的键名。占位符替换适用于设置期间和任务期间通过 HTTPS 443 端口发送的请求；真实凭据不会进入本地进程或文件。</p> <p>保存归环境所有的网络机密后，其目标地址会加入受限互联网访问策略。直接变量和个人值不会增加目标地址。测试前，请检查<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">已保存的网络策略</a>。工作区要求请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a>。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：“管理机密信息”对话框，其中显示一个已遮蔽的注册表令牌、“环境所有”属性，以及 packages.example.com 作为允许访问的目标地址。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"supply-personal-values\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_6\">提供个人值</h3> <p>使用 Personal vault（个人保险库），为你在工作区中的云端环境保存个人环境变量和网络机密。</p> <p>共享环境可以请求每个人从各自账户提供相应的值。分享环境会分享这些值的要求，但不会分享你的个人凭据。</p> <p>系统提示时，在 <strong>Add personal secrets（添加个人机密）</strong> 中填写必需值，然后选择 <strong>Save and start（保存并开始）</strong>。可选值可以留空。</p> <p>如需提前管理这些值：</p> <ol> <li>打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Codex Cloud</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Personal vault（个人保险库）</strong> 标签页。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add（添加）</strong>，在 <strong>Type（类型）</strong> 下选择 <strong>Environment variable（环境变量）</strong> 或 <strong>Network secret（网络机密）</strong>，然后填写相应的 <strong>Key（键）</strong> 和 <strong>Value（值）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Applies to（适用范围）</strong> 下选择 <strong>All environments（所有环境）</strong> 或 <strong>Selected environments（指定环境）</strong>，然后选择 <strong>Save（保存）</strong>。</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>插图：个人保险库对话框中添加环境变量 APP_MODE，值为 development，适用于所有环境。</p> </blockquote> <p>只有任务所请求的值才会传递给任务。针对特定环境设置的值优先于通用默认值。个人网络机密使用该环境允许访问的目标地址，并以相同方式替换占位符。</p> <p><a id=\"share-an-environment-with-your-workspace\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"enterprise\">在 Enterprise 工作区内分享</h2> <p>分享准备好的配置，让同事可以用它开始自己的任务：</p> <ol> <li>打开环境配置。</li> <li>在 <strong>Privacy（隐私）&gt; Who can use（谁可以使用）</strong> 下选择你的工作区。</li> <li>保存更改。如果尚未发布环境，请将其发布。</li> </ol> <p>在 <strong>Who can use（谁可以使用）</strong> 下选择 <strong>Only me（仅我）</strong>，即可将环境设为私有。每项任务都有各自的工作文件；访问配置并不意味着可以访问他人的任务，也不代表有权编辑该环境。</p> <p>分享之前，请检查已准备的文件和归环境所有的凭据。云身份和 VPN 连接也可能提供共享服务访问权限。代码库访问和个人连接则取决于运行任务的账户。</p> <p><strong>Use Codex in the cloud（在云端使用 Codex）</strong> 控制任务访问权限。<strong>Manage workspace environments（管理工作区环境）</strong> 控制谁可以创建和编辑与工作区共享的环境。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=review-codex-cloud-access-and-environment-administration\">角色与工作区权限</a>。</p> <h2 id=\"agent-security\">Agent Security（智能体安全）</h2> <p>环境的<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">互联网访问设置</a>决定其虚拟机可以连接哪些域名。VPN 设置用于将该虚拟机连接到专用网络上的服务。</p> <p>在 Enterprise 工作区中，管理员使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> 配置智能体行为、托管执行网络和受支持工具使用方面的工作区要求。这些要求与每个环境单独保存的域名设置同时生效。Global 策略和受支持的 Codex Cloud 覆盖设置请参阅 Agent Security。</p> <p><a id=\"internet-access-and-network-proxy\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"connect-to-services\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">连接到服务</h2> <p>为工作流程所需的软件包注册表、API 和其他服务配置访问权限：</p> <ol> <li>在环境配置中开启 <strong>Allow Codex to access internet（允许 Codex 访问互联网）</strong>。</li> <li>在 <strong>Allow domains（允许的域名）</strong> 下选择 <strong>Package managers（软件包管理器）</strong> 或 <strong>Custom domains only（仅自定义域名）</strong>，然后在 <strong>Additional allowed domains（其他允许的域名）</strong> 下添加所需主机名。如果工作流程需要更广泛的访问权限，请选择 <strong>All (unrestricted)（全部，不受限制）</strong>。</li> <li>保存设置，并在准备环境期间测试所需服务。发布或重新发布后，再在新任务中验证访问权限。</li> </ol> <p>工作区要求请参阅 <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a>。允许某个目标地址并不会提供凭据，也不会授予该服务本身的权限。</p> <p><a id=\"domains-included-in-the-package-managers-preset\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">“软件包管理器”预设包含的域名</h3> <p><strong>软件包管理器</strong>预设允许访问以下注册表、代码仓库和下载主机：</p> <ul> <li><strong>npm 和 Yarn：</strong> <code>registry.npmjs.org</code>、<code>registry.yarnpkg.com</code></li> <li><strong>PyPI 和 PyTorch：</strong> <code>pypi.org</code>、<code>files.pythonhosted.org</code>、<code>download.pytorch.org</code>、<code>download-r2.pytorch.org</code></li> <li><strong>Rust：</strong> <code>crates.io</code>、<code>index.crates.io</code>、<code>static.crates.io</code>、<code>static.rust-lang.org</code></li> <li><strong>Go：</strong> <code>proxy.golang.org</code>、<code>sum.golang.org</code></li> <li><strong>Maven 和 Gradle：</strong> <code>repo.maven.apache.org</code>、<code>repo1.maven.org</code>、<code>plugins.gradle.org</code>、<code>plugins-artifacts.gradle.org</code>、<code>services.gradle.org</code>、<code>downloads.gradle.org</code></li> <li><strong>Bazel：</strong> <code>bcr.bazel.build</code>、<code>mirror.bazel.build</code></li> <li><strong>Buf：</strong> <code>buf.build</code></li> <li><strong>CPAN：</strong> <code>cpan.metacpan.org</code></li> <li><strong>Ubuntu 和 Debian 软件源：</strong> <code>archive.ubuntu.com</code>、<code>security.ubuntu.com</code>、<code>ports.ubuntu.com</code>、<code>ppa.launchpadcontent.net</code>、<code>deb.debian.org</code>、<code>security.debian.org</code></li> <li><strong>供应商软件源：</strong> <code>packages.microsoft.com</code>、<code>apt.buildkite.com</code>、<code>developer.download.nvidia.com</code>、<code>deb.nodesource.com</code></li> <li><strong>GitHub 源代码、归档、发布文件和 LFS：</strong> <code>github.com</code>、<code>codeload.github.com</code>、<code>github-cloud.githubusercontent.com</code>、<code>github-cloud.s3.amazonaws.com</code>、<code>release-assets.githubusercontent.com</code></li> <li><strong>其他下载站点：</strong> <code>dl.google.com</code>、<code>pkgconfig.freedesktop.org</code></li> </ul> <p>对于已注册的根域名，Codex 也会允许相应的 <code>www</code> 主机名。其他子域名必须分别添加到允许的域名列表中。依赖项需要其他主机时，请将其添加到 <strong>Additional allowed domains（其他允许的域名）</strong>。</p> <p>如果服务位于公共互联网，但会根据来源 IP 筛选连接，请使用 <a href=\"https://openai.com/chatgpt-agents.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">agent egress IP feed（需联网）</a>（智能体出站 IP 列表）。允许列表中应包含已发布的全部地址段；每天检查此列表，并在地址段变化时更新服务的允许列表。这些地址段由多位客户共享；请继续使用服务本身的身份验证和授权控制。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-to-private-services-with-tailscale\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"private-networking-vpn\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"vpn\">专用网络（VPN）</h2> <p>通过 VPN 连接，让云端任务访问专用网络上的内部 API、软件包注册表和其他 HTTP 或 HTTPS 服务。</p> <ol> <li>打开环境的 <strong>Advanced（高级）&gt; VPN</strong> 设置，然后选择 <strong>Add（添加）</strong>。</li> <li>输入 VPN 服务提供商给出的连接凭据。</li> <li>在 VPN 访问规则和环境的<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">互联网访问设置</a>中，分别允许所需目标地址。</li> <li>保存，然后发布或重新发布环境。开始新任务并测试服务。</li> </ol> <p>目前支持的 VPN 服务提供商是 Tailscale。创建 Tailscale 身份验证密钥时，请同时启用 <strong>Reusable（可重用）</strong> 和 <strong>Ephemeral（临时）</strong>。可重用密钥可让新的云端任务虚拟机加入你的网络。Tailscale 会在临时设备离线后自动将其移除。未来计划支持其他 VPN 提供商。</p> <p>支持私有 IPv4 子网路由。任务可以使用 Tailscale 的拆分 DNS（split DNS）和 MagicDNS，通过主机名访问私有服务。</p> <p>如果服务使用组织的内部 DNS，请在 Tailscale 管理控制台中配置拆分 DNS，将发往内部域名的查询转交给你的 DNS 服务器。请使用服务的完全限定主机名（例如 <code>api.corp.example.com</code>），并确认它可以解析到 IPv4 地址。目标地址还必须符合环境的互联网访问设置和 Tailscale 访问规则。</p> <p>使用共享环境的任务会使用其中配置的 VPN 身份。</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-cloud-identity\"></a> <a id=\"configure-an-aws-role-connection\"></a> <a id=\"attach-an-azure-connection\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"access-cloud-resources-with-oidc\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"oidc\">使用 OIDC 访问云资源</h2> <p>OpenID Connect（OIDC）让任务可以取得访问云资源所需的短期凭据。你的组织需要在云服务提供商处配置信任关系，并为该身份授予工作流程所需的权限。</p> <ol> <li>打开已保存环境的 <strong>Advanced（高级）&gt; OIDC</strong> 设置。</li> <li>选择 <strong>Add（添加）</strong>，然后选择可用连接；也可以为受支持的提供商选择 <strong>Create connection…（创建连接……）</strong>。</li> <li>对于新连接，请输入提供商的身份信息并创建连接。然后在提供商一侧使用显示的 <strong>Issuer（签发者）</strong>、<strong>Audience（受众）</strong> 和 <strong>Subject（主体）</strong> 或声明条件配置信任关系，并授予资源权限。</li> <li>确认连接已附加，并检查其别名。保存，然后发布或重新发布环境。</li> <li>开始新任务，分别测试获准和被拒绝的操作。</li> </ol> <p>不同提供商的设置有所不同，而且只能附加受支持的连接。访问权限取决于该身份本身的权限；你的个人提供商权限不会转移给该身份。请在网络策略中分别允许必需的提供商端点和服务目标地址。</p> <p>保存连接附加或别名变更后，这些设置会在环境准备期间生效；要让新任务使用这些设置，还需发布或重新发布环境。编辑共享身份连接可能会影响使用该连接的其他环境。</p> <p>Enterprise 工作区可申请启用 OIDC。请联系 OpenAI 客户团队。</p> <p><a id=\"how-codex-cloud-tasks-run\"></a> <a id=\"how-codex-cloud-chats-run\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"run-and-return-to-a-task\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">运行任务并返回继续</h2> <p>选择已发布的环境并描述目标。Codex 会使用其中的代码库和工具编辑文件、运行命令并检查工作。提交更改或创建拉取请求之前，请检查代码更改和测试结果。</p> <p><a id=\"continue-on-web-or-mobile\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">在网页或移动设备上继续</h3> <p>在网页中选择 <strong>Work in（工作位置）&gt; Cloud（云端）</strong>，然后选择环境。在移动应用中打开 <strong>Codex</strong> 并选择可用环境。请在网页或桌面应用中新建环境。</p> <p>重新打开同一任务，即可跨设备继续工作。新任务会从已发布的配置开始一份独立工作。即使你的电脑处于休眠状态，Codex Cloud 中的任务仍可继续运行。</p> <p><a id=\"start-work-from-a-team-conversation\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-tasks-from-slack-or-microsoft-teams\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"slack-microsoft-teams\">从 Slack 或 Microsoft Teams 启动任务</h3> <p>在启用了云端委派的 Enterprise 工作区中，可以通过 Slack 或 Microsoft Teams 中的 <code>@ChatGPT</code> 请求 Codex 处理代码库。Codex 会使用对话上下文，选择与工作区共享、且任务运行账户有权访问的环境。你可以在提示词中指定首选环境或补充指导。</p> <p>对于使用 Codex Cloud 基于角色访问控制的 Slack 工作区，必须同时向部署的服务账户和提出请求的用户授予 Codex Cloud 访问权限。管理员设置请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\">为 Slack 启用 Codex Cloud</a>。</p> <p>完成连接和审批提示后，请在对话中检查结果。后续请求应由同一个已连接账户提出，才能继续该任务；其他参与者的请求不会自动继续你的任务。</p> <p>有关工作区设置，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=before-you-start\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">管理 ChatGPT in Slack 和 Teams（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>；有关 Slack 任务控制，请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444?anchor=review-approvals-and-results\">在 Slack 中使用 ChatGPT</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"vm-specifications\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">虚拟机规格</h2> <p>每项云端任务都在具有以下默认资源的虚拟机中运行：</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>ChatGPT 套餐</th> <th>vCPU</th> <th>内存</th> <th>磁盘空间</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Plus、Edu Plus</td> <td>2</td> <td>8 GiB</td> <td>8 GiB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pro、Business、Enterprise</td> <td>4</td> <td>16 GiB</td> <td>32 GiB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Edu、Edu Pro</td> <td>4</td> <td>16 GiB</td> <td>32 GiB</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>默认情况下，从上次开始一个轮次或恢复任务起，任务已保存的虚拟机状态最多可恢复七天。</p> <p>Enterprise 可使用更大的虚拟机和自定义规格。有关可用配置和价格，请联系 OpenAI 客户团队。</p> <p><a id=\"current-limitations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_12\">当前限制</h2> <p>云端环境目前不支持以下功能；这些功能已列入未来规划：</p> <ul> <li>电脑和浏览器操作</li> <li>GitLab 和自托管的 GitHub Enterprise Server</li> </ul> <p>存储在代码库中的技能可以在云端任务中使用。个人电脑上的本地技能不会同步到云端环境。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshoot-setup-and-runtime-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_13\">排查设置和运行时访问问题</h2> <p><a id=\"setup-fails-or-a-required-tool-is-missing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">设置失败或缺少必需工具</h3> <p>在设置对话中检查失败的命令。请 Codex 诊断错误，并在修复后重新运行命令。例如：“安装 pnpm 并运行项目测试。”</p> <ul> <li>如果初始设置失败，选择 <strong>Try again（重试）</strong>，即可使用该设置会话中已选的代码库重新尝试。</li> <li>如果修复需要更改源文件、软件包清单或锁文件，请先在编程任务中完成更改，然后返回设置流程。</li> </ul> <p>Codex 验证设置后，请发布或重新发布环境。</p> <p><a id=\"a-package-download-or-https-request-fails\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"https\">软件包下载或 HTTPS 请求失败</h3> <p>分别检查目标主机名和身份验证：</p> <ol> <li>确认环境的<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">互联网访问设置</a>允许访问该主机。例如，如果私有注册表位于 <code>packages.example.com</code>，请检查是否允许了这个准确主机名。如果下载还使用 <code>downloads.example.com</code>，也必须允许访问该主机。</li> <li>检查软件包管理器或客户端配置的 URL 和凭据。允许域名并不会自动授予该服务的访问权限。</li> <li>如果身份验证使用网络机密，请检查其 <strong>Allowed domains（允许的域名）</strong> 是否包含目标地址，并确认请求使用 HTTPS 443 端口。</li> <li>在 Enterprise 工作区中，请管理员同时检查适用的 <a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> 要求和环境设置。</li> </ol> <p>保存配置更改，并在设置期间测试请求。发布或重新发布环境后，再在新任务中验证访问权限。</p> <p><a id=\"a-required-value-is-missing-or-isnt-usable\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_15\">缺少必需值或值无法使用</h3> <p>请确认你在环境配置中的正确位置添加了该值：</p> <ul> <li><strong>环境变量：</strong> 用于程序需要直接读取的值，例如 <code>APP_MODE=development</code>。</li> <li><strong>网络机密：</strong> 用于发往获准 HTTPS 服务的凭据，例如私有注册表令牌。程序会收到占位符；代理会在匹配的请求中替换为真实凭据。如果程序必须直接读取真实值，请将其添加为<strong>环境变量</strong>。</li> </ul> <p>如果使用个人值，请检查其 <strong>Key（键）</strong> 是否与环境要求相同，以及 <strong>Applies to（适用范围）</strong> 是否包含该环境。针对特定环境的值优先于通用默认值。</p> <p>设置说明请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">环境变量和网络机密</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"vpn-connects-but-an-http-or-https-service-is-unreachable\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"vpn-http-https\">VPN 已连接，但无法访问 HTTP 或 HTTPS 服务</h3> <ol> <li>确认客户端使用环境配置的 HTTP/HTTPS 代理。使用 <code>curl</code> 测试时，不要添加 <code>--noproxy</code>，这样请求才会经过该代理。</li> <li>根据环境允许的域名和 VPN 访问规则，分别检查目标地址。</li> <li>如果服务可以通过 IP 地址访问，但无法通过主机名访问，请检查 Tailscale 的 DNS 设置。对于公司内部域名，请确认拆分 DNS 指向正确的 DNS 服务器，且该服务器可通过 Tailscale 网络访问。请使用服务的完全限定主机名，并确认它可以解析到 IPv4 地址。</li> </ol> <p>连接设置请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=private-networking-vpn\">专用网络</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"an-environment-or-its-updates-arent-available-for-a-task\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_16\">任务无法使用环境或其更新</h3> <p>在 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Codex Cloud &gt; Environments（环境）</strong> 中检查环境。如果环境带有 <strong>Unpublished（未发布）</strong> 标记，请完成设置并选择 <strong>Publish（发布）</strong>，使其可用于任务。</p> <p>要更新已发布的环境，请打开其 <strong>Edit（编辑）</strong> 流程，让 Codex 准备并测试更改，然后选择 <strong>Republish（重新发布）</strong>。从更新后的环境开始新任务，才能使用新配置。已有任务保留各自的工作状态。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"cloud-environments\">Cloud environments</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Codex Cloud runs coding tasks in the cloud, so work can continue while your computer is asleep. Use it on the web, on mobile, or in the desktop app to edit code, run commands, and review results.</p> <p>A <strong>cloud environment</strong> is the reusable setup that tasks use: repositories, dependencies, tools, and access settings. Codex inspects your repositories, prepares the setup, and tests it with you. Each new task gets its own isolated workspace from the published environment.</p> <p>For an introduction, see the <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Codex Cloud overview</a>.</p> <p><strong>Codex Cloud (Legacy)</strong> continues to support Code Review and the Linear and GitHub integrations. We plan to deprecate this experience. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-73011d6801bc30d3\">legacy guide</a> to create and manage environments for these workflows.</p> <h2 id=\"start-a-task-in-codex-cloud\">Start a task in Codex Cloud</h2> <p>On the web or in the <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">desktop app</a>, choose <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong> and select a published environment. On mobile, open <strong>Codex</strong> and select a published environment. Describe what you want Codex to do and send the request. If you need a new setup, <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=create-and-publish-an-environment\">create an environment</a> on the web or in the desktop app.</p> <p>Enterprise admins can <a href=\"#/article/a-811aa7aeaf6b8cd4?anchor=step-5-configure-codex-cloud\">review workspace access</a> before rolling out Codex Cloud.</p> <h2 id=\"create-and-publish-an-environment\">Create and publish an environment</h2> <p>Create new environments on the web or in the <a href=\"#/article/a-d6f4398aa4652d7e\">desktop app</a>. Sign in with your ChatGPT account:</p> <ol> <li>In a new task, choose <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong>, open <strong>Select environment</strong>, and select <strong>Create environment</strong>.</li> <li>Select the GitHub repositories to check out. Connect GitHub if prompted.</li> <li>Select <strong>Get started</strong>. Codex inspects the repositories, installs dependencies and tools, and tests the workflow.</li> <li>Supply missing access or information when asked. You can also request specific versions, commands, or services.</li> <li>Review the setup report, configuration, and files. Resolve unfinished work, save changes, and select <strong>Publish</strong>.</li> <li>After <strong>Environment published</strong> appears, select <strong>Start a new task</strong> and describe what you want Codex to do.</li> </ol> <p>You can also start from <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> &gt; <strong>Environments</strong> &gt; <strong>Create environment</strong>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Desktop app environment picker with Create environment and Manage environments below the saved environments</p> </blockquote> <p>Saving stores configuration; some settings apply to the active setup immediately. Publishing captures the prepared filesystem for new tasks. Sharing controls who can use the environment.</p> <p><a id=\"default-universal-image\"></a> <a id=\"automatic-setup\"></a> <a id=\"manual-setup\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"customize-installation-and-startup\">Customize installation and startup</h2> <p>Codex identifies runtimes, package versions, tools, and services from your repositories. Refine the setup in the conversation; you don't need to write an installation script yourself.</p> <p>Codex can record the tested setup in two fields:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Install script:</strong> commands to install dependencies and prepare development assets.</li> <li><strong>Start skill:</strong> instructions to start services and check that they're ready.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Cloud environment setup conversation beside repository, script, network, secret, variable, privacy, and Advanced controls, with Save draft and Publish actions</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"container-caching\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"reuse-and-update-saved-state\">Reuse and update saved state</h2> <ul> <li><strong>New task:</strong> starts from the published environment's prepared filesystem.</li> <li><strong>Existing task:</strong> continues with its own saved files, including uncommitted changes and installed tools.</li> <li><strong>Repository refresh:</strong> runs automatically in the background, preserving dependency caches without rerunning installation or startup commands.</li> </ul> <p>To update the reusable setup, open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> &gt; <strong>Environments</strong>. From the environment's <strong>…</strong> menu, select <strong>Edit</strong>. Describe the change, let Codex prepare and test it, save changes, and select <strong>Republish</strong>. Start a new task to use the update; existing tasks retain their own state.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Codex Cloud settings with Environments and Personal vault tabs and the Edit menu open for a published environment</p> </blockquote> <p>Commit important work or save the output you need. Saved state doesn't replace source control.</p> <p><a id=\"give-setup-access-to-private-dependencies\"></a> <a id=\"prepare-access-to-dependencies-and-services\"></a> <a id=\"environment-variables-and-secrets\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">Configure environment variables and network secrets</h2> <p>Codex identifies missing configuration and asks for values it can't infer. In the environment configuration, select <strong>Manage</strong> beside <strong>Environment variables</strong> or <strong>Network secrets</strong>. Choose how to supply each value:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Configuration</th> <th>Use it for</th> <th>Delivery</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Environment variable</td> <td>A value a program must read directly</td> <td>Passed directly to programs in the environment.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Network secret</td> <td>A credential sent to a specific HTTPS service</td> <td>Programs receive a placeholder; the proxy substitutes the real value for allowed destinations.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>For network secrets, set <strong>Key</strong>, <strong>Value</strong>, and <strong>Allowed domains</strong>. Use a different key from any direct variable. Substitution works for HTTPS on port 443, during setup and tasks; it doesn't put the raw credential in a local process or file.</p> <p>Saving environment-owned network secrets adds their destinations to restricted internet access. Direct variables and personal values don't add destinations. Review the <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">saved network policy</a> before testing. For workspace requirements, see <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a>.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Manage secrets dialog with a masked registry token, Environment ownership, and packages.example.com as its allowed destination</p> </blockquote> <h3 id=\"supply-personal-values\">Supply personal values</h3> <p>Use Personal vault to save your own environment variables and network secrets for cloud environments in your workspace.</p> <p>A shared environment can request values that each person supplies from their own account. Sharing the environment shares these requirements, not your personal credentials.</p> <p>When prompted, enter required values in <strong>Add personal secrets</strong> and select <strong>Save and start</strong>. Optional values can remain unset.</p> <p>To manage values in advance:</p> <ol> <li>Open <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex Cloud</strong>, then select the <strong>Personal vault</strong> tab.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add</strong>, choose <strong>Environment variable</strong> or <strong>Network secret</strong> under <strong>Type</strong>, and enter the matching <strong>Key</strong> and your <strong>Value</strong>.</li> <li>Under <strong>Applies to</strong>, choose <strong>All environments</strong> or <strong>Selected environments</strong>, then <strong>Save</strong>.</li> </ol> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Personal vault dialog adding the APP_MODE environment variable with the value development for all environments</p> </blockquote> <p>Only requested values reach a task. A value for a specific environment takes precedence over a general default. Personal network secrets use the environment's allowed destinations and substitute placeholders in the same way.</p> <p><a id=\"share-an-environment-with-your-workspace\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"share-within-an-enterprise-workspace\">Share within an Enterprise workspace</h2> <p>Share a prepared setup so colleagues can start their own tasks from it:</p> <ol> <li>Open the environment's configuration.</li> <li>Under <strong>Privacy</strong> &gt; <strong>Who can use</strong>, choose your workspace.</li> <li>Save the change. Publish the environment if you haven't already.</li> </ol> <p>Choose <strong>Only me</strong> under <strong>Who can use</strong> to keep the environment private. Each task has separate working files; access to the setup doesn't grant access to someone else's task or permission to edit the environment.</p> <p>Review prepared files and environment-owned credentials before sharing. Cloud identities and VPN connections can also provide shared service access. Repository access and personal connections depend on the account running the task.</p> <p><strong>Use Codex in the cloud</strong> controls task access. <strong>Manage workspace environments</strong> controls creating and editing environments shared with the workspace. See <a href=\"#/article/a-a292ca32ae057ed8?anchor=review-codex-cloud-access-and-environment-administration\">Roles and workspace permissions</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"agent-security\">Agent Security</h2> <p>The environment's <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">internet-access settings</a> define which domains its VM can reach. VPN settings connect that VM to services on a private network.</p> <p>In Enterprise workspaces, admins use <a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> to configure workspace requirements for agent behavior, managed execution networking, and supported tool use. These requirements apply alongside the domain settings saved with each environment. See Agent Security for Global policies and supported Codex Cloud overrides.</p> <p><a id=\"internet-access-and-network-proxy\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"connect-to-services\">Connect to services</h2> <p>Configure access to the package registries, APIs, and other services your workflow needs:</p> <ol> <li>In the environment configuration, turn on <strong>Allow Codex to access internet</strong>.</li> <li>Under <strong>Allow domains</strong>, choose <strong>Package managers</strong> or <strong>Custom domains only</strong>, then add required hosts under <strong>Additional allowed domains</strong>. Use <strong>All (unrestricted)</strong> when the workflow needs broader access.</li> <li>Save and test the services during setup. Publish or republish, then verify access in a new task.</li> </ol> <p>For workspace requirements, see <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=agent-security\">Agent Security</a>. Allowing a destination doesn't supply credentials or grant permissions in that service.</p> <h3 id=\"domains-included-in-the-package-managers-preset\">Domains included in the Package managers preset</h3> <p>The <strong>Package managers</strong> preset allows these registries, repositories, and download hosts:</p> <ul> <li><strong>npm and Yarn:</strong> <code>registry.npmjs.org</code>, <code>registry.yarnpkg.com</code></li> <li><strong>PyPI and PyTorch:</strong> <code>pypi.org</code>, <code>files.pythonhosted.org</code>, <code>download.pytorch.org</code>, <code>download-r2.pytorch.org</code></li> <li><strong>Rust:</strong> <code>crates.io</code>, <code>index.crates.io</code>, <code>static.crates.io</code>, <code>static.rust-lang.org</code></li> <li><strong>Go:</strong> <code>proxy.golang.org</code>, <code>sum.golang.org</code></li> <li><strong>Maven and Gradle:</strong> <code>repo.maven.apache.org</code>, <code>repo1.maven.org</code>, <code>plugins.gradle.org</code>, <code>plugins-artifacts.gradle.org</code>, <code>services.gradle.org</code>, <code>downloads.gradle.org</code></li> <li><strong>Bazel:</strong> <code>bcr.bazel.build</code>, <code>mirror.bazel.build</code></li> <li><strong>Buf:</strong> <code>buf.build</code></li> <li><strong>CPAN:</strong> <code>cpan.metacpan.org</code></li> <li><strong>Ubuntu and Debian repositories:</strong> <code>archive.ubuntu.com</code>, <code>security.ubuntu.com</code>, <code>ports.ubuntu.com</code>, <code>ppa.launchpadcontent.net</code>, <code>deb.debian.org</code>, <code>security.debian.org</code></li> <li><strong>Vendor repositories:</strong> <code>packages.microsoft.com</code>, <code>apt.buildkite.com</code>, <code>developer.download.nvidia.com</code>, <code>deb.nodesource.com</code></li> <li><strong>GitHub source, archives, releases, and LFS:</strong> <code>github.com</code>, <code>codeload.github.com</code>, <code>github-cloud.githubusercontent.com</code>, <code>github-cloud.s3.amazonaws.com</code>, <code>release-assets.githubusercontent.com</code></li> <li><strong>Other downloads:</strong> <code>dl.google.com</code>, <code>pkgconfig.freedesktop.org</code></li> </ul> <p>For registered root domains, Codex also allows the corresponding <code>www</code> hostname. Other subdomains require their own allowed-domain entries. Add any other hosts your dependencies require under <strong>Additional allowed domains</strong>.</p> <p>For services reached over the public internet that filter connections by source IP, use the <a href=\"https://openai.com/chatgpt-agents.json\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">agent egress IP feed (online)</a>. Allow every published range, check the feed daily, and update the service's allowlist when ranges change. These ranges are shared across customers; keep the service's authentication and authorization controls in place.</p> <p><a id=\"connect-to-private-services-with-tailscale\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"private-networking-vpn\">Private networking (VPN)</h2> <p>Give cloud tasks access to internal APIs, package registries, and other HTTP or HTTPS services on your private network through a VPN connection.</p> <ol> <li>Open the environment's <strong>Advanced</strong> &gt; <strong>VPN</strong> settings and select <strong>Add</strong>.</li> <li>Enter the connection credentials from your VPN provider.</li> <li>Allow the required destinations in both your VPN's access rules and the environment's <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">internet-access settings</a>.</li> <li>Save, then publish or republish. Start a new task and test the service.</li> </ol> <p>Tailscale is currently the supported VPN provider. When creating a Tailscale auth key, enable both <strong>Reusable</strong> and <strong>Ephemeral</strong>. A reusable key lets new cloud task VMs join your network. Tailscale automatically removes ephemeral devices after they go offline. Support for additional VPN providers is planned.</p> <p>Private IPv4 subnet routes are supported. Tasks can use Tailscale split DNS and MagicDNS to reach private services by hostname.</p> <p>If your service uses your organization's internal DNS, configure split DNS in the Tailscale admin console to send queries for your internal domain to your DNS server. Use the service's fully qualified hostname, such as <code>api.corp.example.com</code>, which must resolve to an IPv4 address. The destination must also be allowed by the environment's internet-access settings and your Tailscale access rules.</p> <p>Tasks in a shared environment use its configured VPN identity.</p> <p><a id=\"connect-a-cloud-identity\"></a> <a id=\"configure-an-aws-role-connection\"></a> <a id=\"attach-an-azure-connection\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"access-cloud-resources-with-oidc\">Access cloud resources with OIDC</h2> <p>OpenID Connect (OIDC) lets a task obtain short-lived credentials for cloud resources. Your organization configures trust with the cloud provider and grants the identity the permissions the workflow needs.</p> <ol> <li>Open the saved environment's <strong>Advanced</strong> &gt; <strong>OIDC</strong> settings.</li> <li>Select <strong>Add</strong>, then choose an available connection or <strong>Create connection…</strong> for a supported provider.</li> <li>For a new connection, enter the provider's identity details and create it. In the provider, configure trust using the displayed <strong>Issuer</strong>, <strong>Audience</strong>, and <strong>Subject</strong> or claim conditions, and grant resource permissions.</li> <li>Confirm the connection is attached and review its alias. Save, then publish or republish the environment.</li> <li>Start a new task and test an allowed operation and a denied operation.</li> </ol> <p>Provider setup varies, and only supported connections can be attached. The identity's permissions determine access; your personal provider permissions don't transfer to it. Allow the required provider endpoints and service destinations separately in the network policy.</p> <p>Save attachment or alias changes to apply them during setup; publish or republish to use them in new tasks. Editing a shared identity connection can affect other environments that use it.</p> <p>OIDC is available by request for Enterprise workspaces. Contact your OpenAI account team to enable it.</p> <p><a id=\"how-codex-cloud-tasks-run\"></a> <a id=\"how-codex-cloud-chats-run\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"run-and-return-to-a-task\">Run and return to a task</h2> <p>Select a published environment and describe your goal. Codex uses its repositories and tools to edit files, run commands, and check its work. Review changes and test results before committing or opening a pull request.</p> <h3 id=\"continue-on-web-or-mobile\">Continue on web or mobile</h3> <p>On the web, choose <strong>Work in</strong> &gt; <strong>Cloud</strong> and select an environment. On mobile, open <strong>Codex</strong> and choose an available environment. Create new environments on the web or in the desktop app.</p> <p>Reopen the same task to continue its work across devices. A new task starts separate work from the published setup. Tasks in Codex Cloud can keep working while your computer is asleep.</p> <p><a id=\"start-work-from-a-team-conversation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"start-tasks-from-slack-or-microsoft-teams\">Start tasks from Slack or Microsoft Teams</h3> <p>In an Enterprise workspace with Cloud delegation enabled, ask <code>@ChatGPT</code> in Slack or Microsoft Teams to work on a repository. Codex uses the conversation context to choose an environment shared with your workspace and available to the account running the task. You can name a preferred environment or add guidance in your prompt.</p> <p>For Slack, workspaces with Codex Cloud role-based access control must grant Codex Cloud access to both the deployment's service account and the requesting user. See <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?anchor=enable-codex-cloud-for-slack\">Enable Codex Cloud for Slack</a> for admin setup.</p> <p>Complete any connection and approval prompts, then review the result in the conversation. Follow up from the same connected account to continue the task; another participant's request doesn't automatically continue your task.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779?sectionMissing=before-you-start\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">Manage ChatGPT in Slack and Teams (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-6be952b78a5da779\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> for workspace setup and <a href=\"#/article/a-345f9e63361a6444?anchor=review-approvals-and-results\">Use ChatGPT in Slack</a> for Slack task controls.</p> <h2 id=\"vm-specifications\">VM specifications</h2> <p>Each cloud task runs in a VM with these default resources:</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>ChatGPT plan</th> <th>vCPUs</th> <th>Memory</th> <th>Disk space</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Plus, Edu Plus</td> <td>2</td> <td>8 GiB</td> <td>8 GiB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Pro, Business, Enterprise</td> <td>4</td> <td>16 GiB</td> <td>32 GiB</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Edu, Edu Pro</td> <td>4</td> <td>16 GiB</td> <td>32 GiB</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>By default, a task's saved VM state is recoverable for up to seven days after you last start a turn or resume the task.</p> <p>Larger VMs and custom specifications are available for Enterprise. Contact your OpenAI account team for available configurations and pricing.</p> <h2 id=\"current-limitations\">Current limitations</h2> <p>The following capabilities aren't currently supported in cloud environments and are on our roadmap:</p> <ul> <li>Computer and browser use</li> <li>GitLab and self-hosted GitHub Enterprise Server</li> </ul> <p>Skills stored in your repository are available in cloud tasks. Personal skills from your local computer aren't synced to cloud environments.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshoot-setup-and-runtime-access\">Troubleshoot setup and runtime access</h2> <h3 id=\"setup-fails-or-a-required-tool-is-missing\">Setup fails or a required tool is missing</h3> <p>Check the setup conversation for the command that failed. Ask Codex to diagnose the error and rerun the command after fixing it. For example: \"Install pnpm and run the project's tests.\"</p> <ul> <li>If initial setup fails, select <strong>Try again</strong> to retry with the repositories already selected in that setup session.</li> <li>If the fix requires changing source files, a package manifest, or a lockfile, make that change in a coding task, then return to setup.</li> </ul> <p>After Codex verifies the setup, publish or republish the environment.</p> <h3 id=\"a-package-download-or-https-request-fails\">A package download or HTTPS request fails</h3> <p>Check the destination hostname and authentication separately:</p> <ol> <li>Confirm the host is allowed by the environment's <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=connect-to-services\">internet-access settings</a>. For a private registry at <code>packages.example.com</code>, check that exact hostname. If downloads also use <code>downloads.example.com</code>, that host needs access too.</li> <li>Check the package manager or client's configured URL and credentials. Allowing a domain doesn't grant access to the service.</li> <li>If authentication uses a network secret, check that its <strong>Allowed domains</strong> include the destination and that the request uses HTTPS on port 443.</li> <li>In an Enterprise workspace, ask an admin to check the applicable <a href=\"#/article/a-dccd5924f08b9ad8\">Agent Security</a> requirements alongside the environment's settings.</li> </ol> <p>Save any configuration changes and test the request during setup. Publish or republish, then verify access in a new task.</p> <h3 id=\"a-required-value-is-missing-or-isnt-usable\">A required value is missing or isn't usable</h3> <p>Check that you added the value to the right place in the environment configuration:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Environment variables:</strong> use these for values that programs need to read directly, such as <code>APP_MODE=development</code>.</li> <li><strong>Network secrets:</strong> use these for credentials sent to an allowed HTTPS service, such as a private registry token. Programs receive a placeholder; the proxy substitutes the credential in matching requests. If the program needs to read the raw value, add it under <strong>Environment variables</strong>.</li> </ul> <p>For a personal value, check that its <strong>Key</strong> matches the environment's request and that <strong>Applies to</strong> includes that environment. A value for a specific environment takes precedence over a general default.</p> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=configure-environment-variables-and-network-secrets\">Environment variables and network secrets</a> for setup instructions.</p> <h3 id=\"vpn-connects-but-an-http-or-https-service-is-unreachable\">VPN connects, but an HTTP or HTTPS service is unreachable</h3> <ol> <li>Confirm the client uses the environment's configured HTTP/HTTPS proxy. When testing with <code>curl</code>, omit <code>--noproxy</code> so the request uses that proxy.</li> <li>Check the destination against both the environment's allowed domains and the VPN's access rules.</li> <li>If the service is reachable by IP address but not by hostname, check your Tailscale DNS settings. For an internal company domain, verify that split DNS points to the correct DNS server and that the server is reachable through your Tailscale network. Use the service's fully qualified hostname and confirm it resolves to an IPv4 address.</li> </ol> <p>See <a href=\"#/article/a-7ac5ae1c18e03bf1?anchor=private-networking-vpn\">Private networking</a> for connection setup.</p> <h3 id=\"an-environment-or-its-updates-arent-available-for-a-task\">An environment or its updates aren't available for a task</h3> <p>Check the environment in <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Codex Cloud</strong> &gt; <strong>Environments</strong>. If it has an <strong>Unpublished</strong> badge, finish setup and select <strong>Publish</strong> to make it available for tasks.</p> <p>For changes to a published environment, open its <strong>Edit</strong> flow, let Codex prepare and test the changes, then select <strong>Republish</strong>. Start a new task from the updated environment to use the new setup. Existing tasks keep their own working state.</p>"};
